    "name": "Stripped Zucchini",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Striped zucchini (often known as </span><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Cocozelle</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> or Italian Striped) is characterized bya </span><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">distinctive nutty flavor</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\"> and a mild, slightly sweeter taste compared to traditional dark green zucchini. It is widely considered to have a superior, richer flavor, especially when harvested young at 6–8 inches</span></p>",
